<!--
    angr IfElseFlattener (region_simplifiers/ifelse.py), S8 "goto-quality" sub-stage.

    The option-gated ActionIfElseFlatten (option `ifelseflatten`, default-OFF; ELEM
    4103) ports angr's IfElseFlattener: for a 3-component BlockIf whose true-clause
    is statement-terminating (every endpoint returns / aborts, matching angr's
    is_statement_terminating) and whose else-clause is not, it drops the `else` and
    re-parents the former else-body as the if's immediate follower in the parent
    list. A pure print-tree splice (kuna_flatten_ifelse), no p-code cloned.

    Witness (self-contained, no relocations): a function that, after structuring,
    keeps an explicit `else { a0 = 99; }` arm, i.e. a real 3-component BlockIf,
    exactly the shape the pass inspects:

        if (a0 le 0) { if (1 le a1) { do {...} while (...); return a0; } }
        else { a0 = 99; }
        return a0;

    This is the conservative-no-op (honest-partial) invariant the test pins: the
    pass examines this else-bearing BlockIf but correctly declines to flatten it,
    because its true-clause is NOT statement-terminating (it falls through when the
    inner `if (1 le a1)` is false). angr's exact firing predicate (true-terminates
    AND else-does-not) is unmet, so enabling the option is a structural no-op here
    and the output is byte-identical OFF vs ON. Splicing the else away would be
    unsound for a non-terminating true-clause, so refusing it is correct, and that
    safety is what these asserts lock.

    Stage-pipeline note: kuna's region structurer (default-on, DIV-12) and the
    CollapseStructure fallback both already perform terminating-if guard-clause
    flattening natively, so a 3-component BlockIf with a terminating true-clause
    does not arise for ordinary compiler output. The residual the pass targets only
    appears on the ET_REL / undefined-extern witnesses (angr
    test_ifelseflatten_iprule / _clientloop), each gated behind a separate
    loader/function-boundary prerequisite tracked in the sibling [PROPOSAL]
    branches. This test therefore validates the full control surface end-to-end
    (option recognized + registered + catalog) and the no-corruption invariant on a
    real else-bearing function; the splice mechanics proper are covered by the
    BlockGraph unit tests in substrate/block/tests.rs (flatten_ifelse_*).

    Pass 1 (option ifelseflatten off) and Pass 2 (option ifelseflatten on) render
    identically: the explicit `else { a0 = 99; }` survives in both, so each token
    that names the else-bearing form appears exactly twice (once per pass).
-->
